0 Five chain-drive displays compare small gear pairs, a long supported route, a turntable loop and a single gear wrap.
0 Name: TECHNIC_CHAIN_LINK-Constraints.ldr
0 Author: Willy Tschager
0 Unofficial Model
0 // Scene: Two compact coloured loops sit above a long blue chain run. A pale chain curves around a low turntable assembly, while a separate brown loop hugs one gear.
0 // Rigid construction: The principal wheels are 4019 16-tooth, 3648a 24-tooth and 3647 8-tooth gears. Technic bricks and axle pins support the long arrangement; the turntable uses 2855 and 2856.
0 // Build lesson: Show a clear drive route and retain each gear on a supported shaft. Intermediate wheels can reshape the chain envelope without turning the scene into a clutter of unrelated gears.
0 // Reuse: The fourth legacy route gives a tangent warning in the current synthesizer. Tooth engagement, link closure, shaft support and tension still need checking after selecting a smaller study.
0 ROTATION CENTER 0 0 0 1 "Custom" 
0 ROTATION CONFIG 0 0
